 c/di    :      , name,
C===========================================================
C C/DI - integer division, truncating toward zero.
C
C Calling convention for a binary helper:
C   [M15-1] = the dividend, ACC = the divisor
C   M13 = return link
C
C An integer word here carries no exponent, so XORing the
C integer zero into it gives the same value as a real; the AVX
C that follows negates nothing, its operand being the zero word
C at address 0, but the normalization that comes after a
C negation is what A/X wants of its divisor.
C
C The quotient leaves A/X as a real and its fraction has to go.
C Aligning against the integer zero shifts the fraction out, but
C a right shift of a two's complement mantissa goes toward minus
C infinity, which would floor.  So AMX aligns the magnitude
C instead and AVX puts the sign back afterwards: the fraction is
C dropped before the sign returns, which is what makes the
C truncation go toward zero.  That is C/TR's sequence, applied
C to the quotient rather than to an argument, and it leaves the
C mode register at 7 the same way.
C
C The words above the stack top are scratch, for the quotient as
C much as for the divisor: nothing of the caller's lives there.
C===========================================================
                , ntr ,          . normalize and round
            1   , aex , 11b      . =I0  the divisor as a real
                , avx ,          . normalize it for A/X
            15  , stx , 1        . park it above the stack, pop the dividend
            1   , aex , 11b      . =I0  the dividend as a real
                , avx ,          . normalize it too
            15  , a/x , 2        . the real quotient
                , ntr , 3        . suppress normalization and rounding
            15  , atx , 1        . keep the quotient for its sign
            1   , amx , 11b      . =I0  align |q|: the fraction is gone
            15  , avx , 1        . negate it back if the quotient was negative
            1   , aex , 11b      . =I0  strip the integer exponent
            13  , uj  ,
                , end ,
